# NUMERICS: float rendering. `to(str)` is shortest
# round-trip (Ryu-class). Measured: 17 significant digits, so 0.1 renders as
# 0.10000000000000001, and a WHOLE float renders with no fractional part at
# all, making 1.0 indistinguishable from the integer 1.
# expect: 0.10000000000000001 0.33333333333333331 1 1000
# @corpus current
a = 0.1
b = 1.0 / 3.0
c = 1.0
d = 1e3
print("{a} {b} {c} {d}")
